{"title":"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(brute_force)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (brute force)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Right triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/7/c073f8a05257a19c2dacc368858763bb44fa3747.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/d/40db9b6f10ff583906d78a06a76e08e04381bc1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />, have areas of 1 and 2, respectively. A side of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/7/c073f8a05257a19c2dacc368858763bb44fa3747.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> is congruent to a side of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/d/40db9b6f10ff583906d78a06a76e08e04381bc1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />, and a different side of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/7/c073f8a05257a19c2dacc368858763bb44fa3747.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> is congruent to a different side of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/d/40db9b6f10ff583906d78a06a76e08e04381bc1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />. What is the square of the product of the lengths of the other (third) sides of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/7/c073f8a05257a19c2dacc368858763bb44fa3747.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/d/40db9b6f10ff583906d78a06a76e08e04381bc1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/1/6c1dafa3f26ad11b90deeda52b381fb4642153ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{28}{3}\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }10\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }\\frac{32}{3}\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }\\frac{34}{3}\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"410\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First of all, let the two sides which are congruent be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/d/a8d54b3e39757a5100c5b839497b8350d59f8c25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y &gt; x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />. The only way that the conditions of the problem can be satisfied is if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is the shorter leg of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/0/4b034a1760b3fe3a8182c2d2862991d09ebfff30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> and the longer leg of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/6/9168663bdcc2a7840189d9aedc36e824b523cb9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is the longer leg of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/0/4b034a1760b3fe3a8182c2d2862991d09ebfff30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> and the hypotenuse of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/6/9168663bdcc2a7840189d9aedc36e824b523cb9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Notice that this means the value we are looking for is the square of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/c/d2cb4c83c74534a1d030213e1cd6a554549bc28b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{x^{2}+y^{2}} \\cdot \\sqrt{y^{2}-x^{2}} = \\sqrt{y^{4}-x^{4}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"262\" height=\"22\" />, which is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/1/711ec069fafecd8ffd4fa59b8b623687452f303f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^{4}-x^{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>The area conditions give us two equations: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/4/e8478df3f082d318f1fa766ec05bcecc3c2a1a35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{xy}{2} = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"56\" height=\"33\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/6/2d6362040e714120872ae56db2a43286260cb97e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x\\sqrt{y^{2}-x^{2}}}{2} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"119\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p>This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/4/8c4ec7ed986607fe612af146183fa8d5d7df3301.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{4}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"46\" height=\"37\" /> and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/5/0c544c2f8ecf84f7074ed37ca6d1d69c53e78013.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{x^{2}} = y^{2} - x^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"102\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Taking the second equation, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/e/aee18699685a9b712892494bb772fc9bb2d45ca1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2}y^{2} - x^{4} = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"20\" />, so since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/c/27cf2b6cca90cd7da78b22bde20f42f6def98946.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/b/6fb4a68edbda2b33cce3d667799e1db4d48cf689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{4} = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"59\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/4/8c4ec7ed986607fe612af146183fa8d5d7df3301.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{4}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"46\" height=\"37\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/9/379efe8fbff14251131e774eb04028d3168fbdf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^{4} = \\frac{256}{12} = \\frac{64}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"117\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>The value we are looking for is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/9/8c96f17055affc597666d6411052d5eb2f0d378e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^{4}-x^{4} = \\frac{64-36}{3} = \\frac{28}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"188\" height=\"37\" /> so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/8/068950527ac725ac6f06b82fb1a6595647794cff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{28}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"69\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Like in Solution 1, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/4/e8478df3f082d318f1fa766ec05bcecc3c2a1a35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{xy}{2} = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"56\" height=\"33\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/6/2d6362040e714120872ae56db2a43286260cb97e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x\\sqrt{y^{2}-x^{2}}}{2} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"119\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p>Squaring both equations yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/2/8322e14ccac0cf027cb328610888b87222f8bb4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2y^2=16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/9/c19875de8746403a735ac06a58d6efcf677338fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2(y^2-x^2)=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"122\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/8/b589a88bbabbca91ee3367a5f4a1df94e6f850a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = x^2$\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/b/eeb16d26ef59d9469f0572b499926ec9cfcfc60c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/d/d0d547a537e50bc4f2a6f359e8955bd7aec20402.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = \\frac{16}{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"52\" height=\"37\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/6/6468e470fbec34b77c8cfddc81b9309233b00db7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\left(\\frac{16}{a}-a\\right)=4 \\implies 16 - a^2 = 4 \\implies a = 2\\sqrt3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"383\" height=\"43\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/3/3233aefef0bbc0699a7cccc9b7171fe2373d2a2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = \\frac{16}{2\\sqrt3} = \\frac{8\\sqrt3}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"129\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p>We are looking for the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/8/f98fe2abeb68b5d108ded1b120f49c07f2597cc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^4 - x^4 = b^2 - a^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"134\" height=\"18\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/0/dd0e13453ee017b705a5c053175158a7d2f91e0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{64}{3} - 12 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{28}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"156\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Firstly, let the right triangles be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/3/f73bdb8b7afc0d65091ea6f0273651f21a81b8fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EDF$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> being the smaller triangle. As in Solution 1, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8df31e4f6534bde800d7084023fba904b41b9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB} = \\overline{EF} = x$\" width=\"115\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/6/4e6d324da9db4f768ef87fb2b153c1f13faf6ef8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC} = \\overline{DF} = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"116\" height=\"19\" />. Additionally, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/3/3832caa9c34f931673eb46453509a98f5b22a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC} = z$\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/a/60abb11eb9d429b18563c481a8bf670b8db852e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{DE} = w$\" width=\"67\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>We are given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/3/5d37640093fb5ddb4d9d7f1daabda416d9fd8aba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABC] = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/6/786ab70cf288842ec990801d0ff9d1d96253c97a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[EDF] = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"87\" height=\"18\" />, so using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/e/b1e73a55caf9cb88f94f738c8cf38f06c18333e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{area} = \\frac{bh}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"75\" height=\"37\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/9/4497583efd0881a0eec729fd33c3860af19938bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{xy}{2} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"56\" height=\"33\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/7/b176064f7bfe4bee7840bfd73c61be2cffc4e130.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{xw}{2} = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"60\" height=\"33\" />. Dividing the two equations, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/d/ecdd60852a0e6d0b18a1f20e7bcf953e4a3a1c1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{xy}{xw}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"26\" height=\"33\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/7/75776e8dbcb44bd9c1a44f6763763ec9b85010dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{y}{w} = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"50\" height=\"33\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/a/c7a9cf1ca6045a258464163992e344cf193a7522.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 2w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/3/f73bdb8b7afc0d65091ea6f0273651f21a81b8fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EDF$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb4e8f1484876dd33e74dde765bfff59c9e6939.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30^{\\circ}-60^{\\circ}-90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"124\" height=\"16\" /> right triangle, meaning that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/4/a34d58323b91db7c6d5312b120bd4de80c171ebd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = w\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"21\" />. Now by the Pythagorean Theorem in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1947dd2d098034571dd60480ea4ec530e5b67b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(w\\sqrt{3}\\right)^2 + \\left(2w\\right)^2 = z^2 \\Rightarrow 3w^2 + 4w^2 = z^2 \\Rightarrow 7w^2 = z^2 \\Rightarrow w\\sqrt{7} = z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"523\" height=\"35\" />.\n</p><p>The problem requires the square of the product of the third side lengths of each triangle, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/e/90edd1e9f8bb96c4551c5ecf67fd07ec1ffeef6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(wz)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"19\" />. By substitution, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/3480aca46138a454bb35084317f530e672388798.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$wz$\" width=\"22\" height=\"8\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/a/b1af9f3050b08e9dbfe2d6579503e5cd1da66857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(w\\right)\\left(w\\sqrt{7}\\right) = w^2\\sqrt{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"159\" height=\"32\" />. We also know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/1/351d58357c5fa5469849ee7bf9dc04cfd60ac38d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{xw}{2} = 1 \\Rightarrow\\frac{(w)\\left(w\\sqrt{3}\\right)}{2} =1 \\Rightarrow (w)\\left(w\\sqrt{3}\\right) = 2 \\Rightarrow w^2\\sqrt{3} = 2 \\Rightarrow w^2 = \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"583\" height=\"52\" />. \n</p><p>Since we want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/e/bee7a2a129fcfbad329791760b1da5e2ff466d71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(w^2\\sqrt{7}\\right)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"72\" height=\"35\" />, multiplying both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/8/668ab9010c5f466c28fadada8bfeb8151e858602.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" /> gets us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/a/07a1936e6a9fda7568a02bf092e03fa2f7ef52d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w^2\\sqrt{7} = \\frac{2\\sqrt{21}}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"114\" height=\"41\" />. Now squaring gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/0/440ed5a96032192d325b78d8a632436e74aaf760.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{2\\sqrt{21}}{3}\\right)^2 = \\frac{4*21}{9} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }\\frac{28}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"248\" height=\"56\" />.\n</p><p>[Note: there is a mismatch of variables near the beginning that someone can fix: xw/2 is the area of the small triangle, which is actually the 30-60-90.]\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28brute_force.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(brute_force)\">Solution 4 (brute force)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (brute force)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This is a little more tedious than the other solutions, so it isn't preferable to be used in \ncompetition, but can be used if needed. We draw the two triangles, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e9e8b2c23e0545ef6de81f0ea578173e9ab7a64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DEF$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, such that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/3/5d37640093fb5ddb4d9d7f1daabda416d9fd8aba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABC] = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/4/4247bcaeecedfd0bd9199a92032efa021d62dfd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[DEF] = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"90\" height=\"20\" />. We denote the two sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e9e8b2c23e0545ef6de81f0ea578173e9ab7a64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DEF$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are \nnaturally the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> shortest sides, both the legs. But for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, we would want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> to be equal \nto one of its legs and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> to be equal to the hypotenuse, to make the 2nd leg shorter (to make \nits area equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />). \n</p><p>So the 2nd leg's equation is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08d0ff48552f918fb4813f670024af8ecc65a469.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{x^2 - y^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"24\" /> (using pythagorean theorem), and the \nhypotenuse of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/6/c0688227c7a4c52edfc3dfbb79cf828c9e555c94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{x^2 + y^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"22\" />. So we are trying to find \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/9/409258a22b4b13f063a89addec36aa98d275239b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{x^2 - y^2} \\cdot \\sqrt{x^2 + y^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"165\" height=\"24\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/0/c406fee9ea4a4b36bdf6d0f1194514b346491435.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{x^2 - y^2} \\cdot \\sqrt{x^2 + y^2} = \\sqrt{(x^2 - y^2)(x^2+y^2)} = \\sqrt{x^4-y^4}\\]\" width=\"445\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>Now, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/0/4a08c4c1431ba612a7f5f04de67b275518a068b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ABC]=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"88\" height=\"20\" />, so using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/3/3731ea13f21b5d1d525035235e8a2ced35228c39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{b \\cdot h}{2}=A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"75\" height=\"39\" />, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/5/915882f35dbf71904a9f17971ab30daac4b4ec67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{x^2 - y^2} \\cdot y}{2}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"134\" height=\"42\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/7/a675c213de8957ef1b7d625cbcc0bdd3e3a0d19b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{x^2 - y^2} \\cdot y=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"24\" />. \n</p><p>We also know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/d/84df6a1603bbaced4769ce98a433b0948b0d737e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[DEF]=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"90\" height=\"20\" />, so:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/1/8611e8862e2fe87c435e765280d1283374ea58a9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{xy}{2}=2 \\implies xy=4 \\implies x=\\frac{4}{y}\\]\" width=\"254\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>We substitute into our first equation, to get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/6/df64d9eb69d99188432040473a4cdce357c8626c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{4}{y}\\right)^2 - y^2} \\cdot y=2\\]\" width=\"158\" height=\"53\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/3/7a3028fec8fe780aa3d418fb6863aca3777a181d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies \\sqrt{\\frac{16}{y^2} - y^2} \\cdot y=2\\]\" width=\"173\" height=\"53\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/e/e3e907e72c1e22c5247dee0298d84786ec51d9b2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies \\sqrt{\\frac{16-y^4}{y^2}} \\cdot y=2\\]\" width=\"173\" height=\"53\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/2/0f2ab69b9aca0093fae4e139379bf68fc8d8d3b6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies \\frac{\\sqrt{16-y^4}}{y} \\cdot y=2\\]\" width=\"170\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/c/0ac66750abc95551db4bc1a14a3764047315a880.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies \\sqrt{16-y^4}=2 \\implies 16-y^4=4 \\implies y^4=12 \\implies y=12^{\\frac{1}{4}}\\]\" width=\"505\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>We plug this into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/3/793253cf2350a96b536ce985558b606b57232120.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/6513cea2add7a75a1e870ba12f6e51b28421af44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\left(12^{\\frac{1}{4}}\\right)=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"98\" height=\"34\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/d/8cddceb3d4e700e74e2b3c73ed9629a7fa00ee65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{4}{12^{\\frac{1}{4}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"69\" height=\"40\" />. \nWe raise both sides to the 4th power, giving us:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/1/db1cebc3cc2ed4d4a581f8538403248e637a1389.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^4=\\frac{256}{12} \\implies x^4=\\frac{64}{3}\\]\" width=\"185\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Now we can put this into our <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/6/db6e942c8c56c13e1842c37386353e7ad91d46bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{x^4-y^4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"24\" /> equation, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/5/385562be0cbadf4cab7121f82b67015e3d921db8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^4=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/7/f67b97a795c537714888bc3b46cbe6dc40c5ee05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^4=\\frac{64}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"66\" height=\"38\" />, to get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/c/cac543fe92a0e8330b08ac283ae06c60f88d4e14.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{\\frac{64}{3}-12} \\implies \\sqrt{\\frac{64}{3}-\\frac{36}{3}} \\implies \\sqrt{\\frac{28}{3}}\\]\" width=\"302\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>But remember that the problem is asking for the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/666e40e457c5de9abc853f721fe80b579e55d741.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textit{square}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"12\" /> of the product of the 3rd side, \nso we square our product:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/d/3fde1a11ca8b6c3dcecc0f18d26de22e7ac21213.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies \\left(\\sqrt{\\frac{28}{3}}\\right)^2\\]\" width=\"112\" height=\"57\" />\n</p><p>to finally get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/4/c646d5a9c2fbbb996843ac434ad33347df52b1b7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } \\frac{28}{3}}\\]\" width=\"69\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>- naman14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Set the length of the smaller leg of the triangle with area 1 as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and the hypotenuse as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />. The two sides of this triangle that are congruent to the triangle with area 2 are going to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/f/48f1f1ed87c5be2d0007485686548a028265d14e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{b^2-a^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"72\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, because if one of the shared side lengths was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> then the other leg of the second triangle would have to be both the same length as the hypotenuse of triangle one and double the length of the bigger leg, which isn't possible because the longer leg of a right triangle can't be half of the hypotenuse.\n</p><p><br />\nThe area of triangle 1 is half of triangle 2 so we can have an equation now:\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/f/bff29bfca50624901e4b6f0050bc7c2b2f9c5776.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a\\cdot\\sqrt{b^2-a^2}=\\sqrt{b^2-a^2}\\cdot b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"218\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/3/a2351747c6dd7a122eb371a579659aefb5342ac0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a=b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><br />\nIf the hypotenuse is double the length of the small leg, that means the first triangle is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/c/47c78b85058ee5e17f88e2cde302e48aad826b35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30-60-90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"15\" /> triangle. To find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, we can relate it to the area of the first triangle.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/4/944e990289006dffa095b1570132f9049c221cc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a\\cdot\\sqrt{3}a}{2}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"96\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/9/ca9bab6a24ca5fdc8f40dae292a3cde1996869de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\cdot\\sqrt{3}a=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c163a7e82ebcbdd6187bbe47c7141a76bb421dc1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"71\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Now that we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/9/9698c992334be77221be8c8c819909eca34fde9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> we can find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/d/a1d03c3c5b9abf1bdb0c9df06fe5fb11ae13d0e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" /> by multiplying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/9/9698c992334be77221be8c8c819909eca34fde9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/d/2bd0d869b41e353aeda1dddad0d3c926a42ad7ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2=\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"70\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>We can find the square of the hypotenuse of the second triangle(the third side) if we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/9/9698c992334be77221be8c8c819909eca34fde9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/d/a1d03c3c5b9abf1bdb0c9df06fe5fb11ae13d0e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/3/bd30c59f1e9550a1107c671159fe5f7520d29f67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2b^2-a^2=\\frac{16}{\\sqrt{3}}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}=\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"221\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><br />\nThe problem asks us to multiply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/9/9698c992334be77221be8c8c819909eca34fde9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> by the number we just got to get the answer.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/9/9795beb43875826f90f104cc48865616b949f84c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{3}}=\\frac{28}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"118\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><br />\nAnd we're done(read in Richard Rusczyk voice).\n</p><p><br />\n-BOTNATE\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/mXvetCMMzpU\">https://youtu.be/mXvetCMMzpU</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B\">2019 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php